<refentry id="sql-alterstorageserver">
 <indexterm zone="sql-alterstorageserver">
  <primary>ALTER STORAGE SERVER</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>ALTER STORAGE SERVER</refentrytitle>
  <manvolnum>7</manvolnum>
  <refmiscinfo>SQL - Language Statements</refmiscinfo>
 </refmeta>

 <refnamediv>
  <refname>ALTER STORAGE SERVER</refname>
  <refpurpose>change the definition of a storage server</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>

 <refsynopsisdiv>
<synopsis>
ALTER STORAGE SERVER <replaceable>name</replaceable> OPTIONS ( [ ADD | SET | DROP ] <replaceable>option</replaceable> [ '<replaceable>value</replaceable>' ] [, ... ] )
ALTER STORAGE SERVER <replaceable>name</replaceable> OWNER TO { <replaceable>new_owner</replaceable> | CURRENT_ROLE | CURRENT_USER | SESSION_USER }
</synopsis>
 </refsynopsisdiv>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Description</title>
  <para>
   <command>ALTER STORAGE SERVER</command> changes a storage server's options
   or owner. Storage servers are shared by all databases in the cluster.
  </para>
  <para>
   You must own the storage server to alter it. To change its owner, you must
   also be able to <command>SET ROLE</command> to the new owning role.
   A superuser can change the owner
   of any storage server. Changing ownership preserves the server's options
   and adjusts its access privileges for the new owner.
  </para>
  <para>
   Use <command>COMMENT ON STORAGE SERVER</command> to add or replace a
   description. The comment is visible from every database in the cluster.
   The storage server's owner or a superuser can change its comment; specifying
   <literal>NULL</literal> or an empty string removes the comment.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Examples</title>
<programlisting>
ALTER STORAGE SERVER archive OWNER TO archive_admin;
COMMENT ON STORAGE SERVER archive IS 'Storage for archived files';
COMMENT ON STORAGE SERVER archive IS NULL;
</programlisting>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Compatibility</title>
  <para>
   <command>ALTER STORAGE SERVER</command> is an Apache Cloudberry extension.
  </para>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>
